WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.220
the the royal tombs of the new kingdom
appear to be models of the netherworld

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.640
we actually know this because the
architecture of the tombs matches the

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.019
architecture of the netherworld
in the book of the hidden chamber the

00:00:33.019 --> 00:00:38.329
text that we often refer to as the Amduat
so on the walls of some of the tombs are

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:44.629
a type of Illustrated religious text
prototype for the very architecture of

00:00:44.629 --> 00:00:50.960
those tombs when we think about Egyptian
funerary texts I think most people

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.409
think about The Book of the Dead which
the ancient Egyptians called The Book of

00:00:54.409 --> 00:00:58.879
going forth by day but there's a whole
additional tradition that we have to

00:00:58.879 --> 00:01:02.689
talk about that culminates in the New
Kingdom royal tombs in the Valley of the

00:01:02.689 --> 00:01:08.600
Kings so it actually starts as early as
the fifth dynasty the final king of the

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:13.909
fifth dynasty a king named Unas is the
first king to have Pyramid Texts so to

00:01:13.909 --> 00:01:20.329
have spells and rituals written down
inside his burial chamber and then those

00:01:20.329 --> 00:01:26.060
pyramid texts many of them continue into
the coffin texts which then continued into

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:30.350
the Book of the Dead with additional
spells added but the netherworld books

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:34.549
are an entirely separate tradition so
you can't really say that the Pyramid

00:01:34.549 --> 00:01:38.450
Texts become the coffin texts become the
book of the dead although some spells

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:42.950
actually do that like new ones come in
as we go new ones coming in and some

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:48.740
stay the same this kind of architecture
and text relating that there being a

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:53.179
significance not just of what a text
says but where the text says it and

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:59.179
that's why reading texts out of books can
be somewhat misleading because those

00:01:59.179 --> 00:02:03.289
texts in a book on the pages are in
three dimensions in the original

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:06.409
Monument
so getting to see what they look like

00:02:06.409 --> 00:02:10.729
and some of the amazing 3d models that
are being made available now through the

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:14.569
Ministry of Antiquities in Egypt you get
a sense to be there you get a sense of

00:02:14.569 --> 00:02:19.190
what it's like to be surrounded by these
texts in a larger architectural setting

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:22.700
another interesting thing to point out
is that there isn't an idea that there

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:27.320
is a single there's a book of the
Pyramid Texts and that's it because each

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.640
pyramid has a
slightly different grouping and

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:35.170
additional text may come in and some
text may not appear again or may not

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:39.040
appear in that particular Monument and
when we look at the netherworld books

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:44.769
that becomes overwhelmingly significant
because the book of Amduat you will

00:02:44.769 --> 00:02:49.209
also hear about the book of gates the
book of caverns the book of the earth

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:54.819
also known as creation of the solar disk
all that these texts describe the same

00:02:54.819 --> 00:02:58.840
twelve hours of the night
but in radically different ways there

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:04.629
are overlaps particularly on Amduat and
Gates but there's also these huge

00:03:04.629 --> 00:03:09.099
divergences and for the Egyptians it's
not as if one is right one is wrong one

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:13.090
is from one place one is from one group
of priests but they take a multiplicity

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:18.519
of approaches when thinking about
something that is by its very nature the

00:03:18.519 --> 00:03:21.970
beyond the interesting thing about the
netherworld books is that although they

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:25.720
are concerned with the Duat although
they are concerned with the nocturnal

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:31.739
journey of the Sun they are in many ways
primarily a solar text and they revolve

00:03:31.739 --> 00:03:36.010
frequently if not exclusively some of
them around this concept of

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:41.230
reconciliation of life and death the
joining of the god Osiris who is equated

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:46.629
with yesterday and the god ray who is
tomorrow the male/female elements of the

00:03:46.629 --> 00:03:51.910
solar disk the aton, and the khat, the
corpse the horizon the akhet as the

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:57.430
female elements this reconciliation of
cosmic opposites to achieve maat that

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:09.699
brings about rebirth a number of the
royal tombs have been open really since

00:04:09.699 --> 00:04:14.349
the end of the New Kingdom
apparently during the greco-roman period

00:04:14.349 --> 00:04:20.620
when a lot of visitors came to Egypt
became a tourist attraction the tombs

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:26.050
were visited there are a number of
greco-roman graffiti in the tombs and

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:34.690
the Greek term for a tomb in the Valley
of the Kings was syrinx a flute a long tube -

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:38.430
going into the
mountain side the Greeks named Egyptian

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:43.919
things rather odd terms sometimes like
obelisk the sky piercing tekhen is

00:04:43.919 --> 00:04:52.889
called in Greek obelisk meaning a meat
skewer a roosting spit kebab stick I

00:04:52.889 --> 00:04:58.710
love this idea of greco-roman tourists
and we know that there were guides that

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:05.819
local Egyptian priests would give tours
of Egyptian monuments Herodotus and his

00:05:05.819 --> 00:05:10.680
Histories records talking to priests and
getting tours of ancient sites so just

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:16.430
how tourists today visit the Valley of
the Kings in Greek times and Roman times

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:21.750
visitors would have gone and
unfortunately this idea of graffiti

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:27.690
izing of adding your name to an ancient
monument has a multi thousand year

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:32.789
history in the greco-roman period the
tomb of Ramses the 6th seems to have

00:05:32.789 --> 00:05:36.930
been one of the more popular places to
visit and it was actually known as the

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:42.719
tomb of metempsychosis as though there
was a concept of wandering of the soul

00:05:42.719 --> 00:05:46.789
and ancient Egypt as though they were
possibly even some concept of

00:05:46.789 --> 00:05:51.960
reincarnation that doesn't really seem
to come out of the Egyptian text as such

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:58.500
but the tombs did receive name so Ramses
the 6th tomb for instance is treated in

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:04.229
some texts I believe is the tomb of
memnon and all of the West Bank would

00:06:04.229 --> 00:06:10.770
even be called the Memnonia the realm of
eMmnon possibly based on epithets of

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:16.440
some of the pharaohs is "mery Amun" and
beloved of Amun that's fascinating and the

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:21.180
two really famous statues of Amunhotep
the 3rd the colossi often erroneously

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:27.360
called the colossi of memnon is only one
colossus exactly only one only the North

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:33.180
Colossus was actually memnon so both of
the colossi were in front of the

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:39.719
mortuary temple of Amunhotep the 3rd who
had a golden age in his 38th year reign

00:06:39.719 --> 00:06:44.159
although his tomb in the Valley of the
Kings is fairly rarely visited because

00:06:44.159 --> 00:06:48.480
it was in the West Valley so this idea
of a

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:52.860
sacred statue was interesting because
although in the greco-roman period the

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:58.110
northern colossus of Amunhotep the
third was called memnon the leader of

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:02.340
the Ethiopian contingent fighting for
the Trojans even though the northern

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:07.080
statue is the divine image in the
greco-roman period we know from

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:13.590
inscriptions on the backs of the colossus
of the southern Colossus that the

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:18.780
southern statute when erected in the
reign of Amunhotep the third the southern

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:25.080
statue has its own name and is a
divinity in its own right by whom the

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:30.530
king himself may be said to be beloved
and this brings up a really interesting

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:35.070
ancient Egyptian practice which is the
ritual of the opening of the mouth and

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:38.160
this is something that we see in the New
Kingdom royal tombs it is certainly

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:43.050
something that we see in private tombs
and you could perform the ritual of

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:47.250
opening the mouth both on the mummy
which is how we traditionally think

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:54.330
about it as well as a statue so for the
Egyptians doing this ritual of the adze

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:58.550
that's being touched to the mouth of
either the statue or the mummy that

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:04.110
enables the mummy or the statute to
receive the spirit of the deceased or

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:09.210
the spirit of the reigning king this
goes to the heart of ancient Egyptian

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:15.930
practice that an image of representation
of a person or a king or a God could

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:23.630
receive the divine spirit

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:28.800
when you walk into an ancient Egyptian
royal tomb in the Valley of the Kings

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:33.450
you go through a series of descending
passageways and the architecture beyond

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:37.260
that can incorporate the angle change
that we see in the 18th dynasty or

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:43.890
simply a jog in this series of
descending corridors and the very first

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:51.510
corridor is called the path of Shu now
Shu is the god of light and space we

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:56.940
could even say the god of luminous space
and he is the god who stands between Geb

00:08:56.940 --> 00:09:01.920
a God who can personify the earth and
Nut a goddess who can personify the sky

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:08.580
and remember that these tombs would have
only been visited during the actual

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:12.870
funerary ceremonies as well as by
medjoy who patrolled the Valley of the

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:17.360
Kings and check to make sure that
nothing had been disturbed in the tombs

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:22.709
but otherwise they were sealed the
rituals the ceremonies those were taking

00:09:22.709 --> 00:09:28.080
place in the mortuary temple but at the
same time those first two corridors of

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:33.360
the pathway of Shu are where we see
representations of the forms of the Sun

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:38.880
and a text that we call the book of Adoring Re in the West or commonly

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:42.570
called the Litany of Re, the first is
the ancient title the other is the

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:47.540
conventional modern title the
netherworld books as we call them that

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:53.010
adorn the walls of primarily the royal
tombs of the New Kingdom although they

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:58.020
have occurred elsewhere and later as
well these texts we call the netherworld

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:04.620
books begin to appear around the time of
hatshepsut and Thutmose III she's a

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:09.089
great innovator she does seem to be we
have blocks associated with one of the

00:10:09.089 --> 00:10:14.250
burials of Thutmose the first that have
the book of Amduat on them the book

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:18.540
of the hidden chamber and then we also
see both the book of the hidden chamber

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:24.000
and the book of Adoring in the West
in the tomb of Useramun Thutmose the

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:27.750
Third's vizier which is one of the very
few times we see it in a private  tomb - and

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:32.610
it's interesting that the book of the
hidden chamber contains directions as to

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:37.620
how it is to be laid
out on wall and it also contains some

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:42.540
instructions as to how to lay out
apparently this index that appears along

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:47.430
with it and it's rather interesting
composition we don't really know the

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:50.970
origins of these texts some people have
tried to push them back much farther

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:55.500
than their earliest occurrences others
assume they probably date to just about

00:10:55.500 --> 00:11:00.450
the time of the earliest occurrence
grammatically it doesn't seem likely

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:07.710
that they existed in their present form
prior to the Middle Kingdom and this is

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:11.520
an important point as well that when we
think about funerary texts in ancient

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:16.260
Egypt most people would think Book of
the Dead that that's the classic the

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:21.410
papyrus scrolls with various spells
showing you how to pass the gates

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:27.779
transformed into a scarab go through the
judgment hall chapter 125 where your

00:11:27.779 --> 00:11:32.730
heart is weighed against the feather of
truth against Maat but that's a separate

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:37.890
tradition from the netherworld books so
the Book of the Dead can occur in New

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:42.240
Kingdom royal tombs in the Valley of the
Kings but it's a much smaller percentage

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:47.580
of the wall space right it says I mean
interestingly on the second shrine of

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:51.410
Tutankhamun that contains one of the
three versions of a cryptographic

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:56.459
netherworld book that revolves around
this concept of the union of Re and

00:11:56.459 --> 00:12:01.290
Osiris we get a mixture of cryptographic
netherworld text and book the dead

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:07.200
passages so there are just hieroglyphs
there are cryptographic hieroglyphs

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:19.860
right and we'll talk about that later!

